    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I've fixed the floating-point precision bug! Here's what I changed:\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen converting \"39.95\" to cents, JavaScript computes `39.95 * 100 = 3995.0000000000005` (not an integer). Your validation checks `Number.isInteger(price)`, which fails.\n\n**The Solution:**\nI added `Math.round()` to all three price-parsing functions to ensure results are always clean integers:\n\n- `parseEuros()` in `src/money.js` \n- `cellCents()` in `src/money.js`\n- `decimalCommaToCents()` in `src/locale.js`\n\n**Testing:**\n- All 50 existing tests pass \u2713\n- Gym 39.95 now adds successfully \u2713  \n- Netflix 12.99 and Spotify 10.99 still work \u2713\n- Edge cases like 1.95, 0.99, 49.95, 99.99 all work \u2713\n\nReady to commit?",
